An unlock that hands a mutex to the thread that waited least, not most.
A thread holds a mutex it neither took nor was the first in line for.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a thread came to hold a mutex neither by its own lock nor as the one that waited longest

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -646,7 +646,7 @@ static struct thread *mutex_give(struct mutex *m)
     m->holder = 0;
     struct thread *w = NULL;
     if (m->waiters != 0) {
-        w = p2v(m->waiters);
+        w = p2v(((struct thread *)p2v(m->waiters))->queue_prev);
         ring_remove(&m->waiters, w);
         w->waiting_on = 0;
         w->flags &= (uint8_t)~THREAD_LENDS;
